{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the smallest positive multiple of 450 whose digits are all zeroes and ones, we need to consider the factors of 450. The prime factorization of 450 is:\n\n\\[ 450 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 5^2 \\]\n\nThis means that any multiple of 450 must be divisible by 2, 9, and 25. Let's analyze these conditions one by one.\n\n1. **Divisibility by 2**: A number is divisible by 2 if its last digit is even. Since the digits of our number can only be 0 or 1, the last digit must be 0.\n2. **Divisibility by 9**: A number is divisible by 9 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 9. Since the digits are only 0 or 1, the sum of the digits is the number of 1's in the number. Therefore, the number of 1's must be a multiple of 9.\n3. **Divisibility by 25**: A number is divisible by 25 if its last two digits are 00, 25, 50, or 75. Since the only digits allowed are 0 and 1, the last two digits must be 00.\n\n","prefix_end":889,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,24632,6785,5248,315,220,19,20,15,6693,18509,525,678,97443,323,6174,11,582,1184,311,2908,279,9363,315,220,19,20,15,13,576,10250,8168,2022,315,220,19,20,15,374,1447,78045,220,19,20,15,284,220,17,1124,15136,220,18,61,17,1124,15136,220,20,61,17,1124,2533,1986,3363,429,894,5248,315,220,19,20,15,1969,387,74916,553,220,17,11,220,24,11,323,220,17,20,13,6771,594,23643,1493,4682,825,553,825,382,16,13,3070,12509,285,3147,553,220,17,95518,362,1372,374,74916,553,220,17,421,1181,1537,15723,374,1496,13,8704,279,18509,315,1039,1372,646,1172,387,220,15,476,220,16,11,279,1537,15723,1969,387,220,15,624,17,13,3070,12509,285,3147,553,220,24,95518,362,1372,374,74916,553,220,24,421,279,2629,315,1181,18509,374,74916,553,220,24,13,8704,279,18509,525,1172,220,15,476,220,16,11,279,2629,315,279,18509,374,279,1372,315,220,16,594,304,279,1372,13,15277,11,279,1372,315,220,16,594,1969,387,26